From f90eab3ed7ea3b6782dfd9a845a74144bd266117 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilan Joselevich <personal@ilanjoselevich.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:20:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] workers: report failure and drain reasons, disk and
 substituter traffic

A builder knows more than the scheduler hears. It gets Nix's
BuildResult, with a status such as TimedOut and an error that ends with
the build log's last lines, and sends only FAILED. It knows why it takes
no builds, stopping, low disk or a local nix-daemon that does not
answer, and sends only draining. It knows its free disk and what it
downloads from each substituter, and reports neither.

Done now carries Nix's status, and for FAILED the error text. The
builder removes ANSI escapes, masks common secret shapes (URL userinfo,
secret query values, Authorization headers, Bearer tokens, secret-named
variables and quoted keys, private key blocks), then cuts the text to
4096 bytes as the first two lines, "[...]" and the end. A failure
without a BuildResult is STATUS_WORKER_ERROR with the error message.
Load carries the reason too, stopping first, then low disk, then the
local nix-daemon, and goes out again when the reason changes. A Load
that does not change whether a worker drains no longer wakes Envoy's
watchers or runs a dispatch pass.

A logger that wraps nix::logger tallies the nix-daemon's substitution
activities per substituter: NAR bytes, wire bytes, paths that arrived
whole and substitutions that stopped short. URLs are cut to
scheme://host[:port]/path. Builders stat the store's file system every
tick and send a WorkerReport with free disk and the new traffic, at most
every 2 s and only when something changed, to a scheduler that asked
with ReportsWanted.

The scheduler passes all of it to watchers. DrvGone gets the status and
the error text, which the scheduler makes valid UTF-8, strips of control
and bidi characters, masks and cuts again. WorkerState gets the drain
reason, the builder's version, free and total disk, --min-free and the
traffic per substituter, and Counters sums the traffic over builders. A
report updates the counters at once and runs no dispatch pass. The
scheduler cancels a Watch stream with more than 4 MiB of failure text
queued, and ends a message once its text reaches 1 MiB, so messages stay
under gRPC's 4 MiB receive limit. --niks3-cache-url names the farm cache
as builders substitute from it.

New metrics:
nix_grpc_substituter_{nar_bytes,download_bytes,paths,failures}_total,
nix_grpc_store_free_bytes, nix_grpc_store_size_bytes and
nix_grpc_min_free_bytes on builders, and
nix_grpc_sched_failures_total{reason} and the draining kinds of
nix_grpc_sched on the scheduler.

build-report-test covers the status names, the masks and the cut, and
builder-test the reason in each Load. Older schedulers ignore the new
fields. Older builders send none, and their status reads unreported.
